281→/// Get the flag to pass commands to the shell.
282→///
283→/// Uses `-lic` (interactive login shell) on Unix so that the user's
284→/// full shell environment is available. Tools like mise, asdf, nvm,
285→/// and rbenv are typically activated in `.zshrc`/`.bashrc` (interactive)
286→/// or `.zprofile`/`.bash_profile` (login). Without `-lic`, these tools
287→/// aren't in PATH and step commands fail with "command not found".
288→///
289→/// In CI environments, uses `-lc` (login, non-interactive) to avoid
290→/// `bash: cannot set terminal process group` errors caused by `-i`
291→/// trying to set up job control without a TTY.
292→fn shell_flag(_shell: &str) -> &'static str {
293→    if cfg!(target_os = "windows") {
294→        "/C"
295→    } else if super::is_ci() {
296→        "-lc"
297→    } else {
298→        "-lic"
299→    }
300→}
